WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.350
Behind the scenes, three things matter.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.784
Processing engines decide which server
does which work, so you can keep, say,

3
00:00:06.784 --> 00:00:11.362
public certificate requests on one server
that's allowed out to the internet.

4
00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:14.371
The log servers record
every event and are the

5
00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:17.538
only servers that need a
path to the SIEM and email.

6
00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:21.871
And the message bus keeps every
server informed about changes,

7
00:00:21.871 --> 00:00:24.788
which means one firewall rule people miss:

8
00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:29.038
port 8883 has to be open between
every server, across sites too.

9
00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:33.410
Watch distance as well — every server
works against one active database,

10
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.350
and at a thirty-millisecond delay a single
renewal takes about fifteen seconds.
